note Each tab in a panel's header has a close icon after its name. Pressed, that view leaves the layout: the panel shows its next tab (or the one before, at the end), and a panel left with no tabs closes, its sibling taking the room, the same as dragging its last tab away. The last panel of the window never closes; it stays empty with the hint to press +. A closed view comes back through + or when navigation needs it (opening a path brings back Path, a search Results). The change is saved with the layout.

